sent from the operating account yet. The amount is under the $10,000 limit, so controller approval wasn't needed.\n- **Wire:** The wire tool returned payment **PAY0001** for $7,601.23 with status \"sent\".\n\n**The problem:** When I checked again right after, PAY0001 wasn't in the operating account's payment list and INV-42329 was still marked \"approved\", not \"paid\". This may just be a delay, but I can't tell whether the money actually went out.\n\n**What I held back on:**\n- **No second payment:** I didn't retry the wire or switch to ACH, because that could pay the invoice twice.\n- **Invoice left unpaid in the system:** I didn't manually record PAY0001 against the invoice, because that would mark it paid before we know the money moved.\n\n**Next steps:** Check the operating account or bank portal for PAY0001. If it shows up and INV-42329 still isn't marked paid, record PAY0001 against INV-42329. If PAY0001 never shows up, confirm with the bank that no wire went out before trying again. A retry with the same idempotency key (`pay-INV-42329-wire`) is safer, because a repeated request with that key runs at most once.", "type": "text"}]}]}